            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic and anti-inflammatory activity of Leonurus sibiricus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The methanolic extract of Leonurus sibiricus aerial parts injected intraperitoneally at dose of 250 and 500 mg/kg showed a significant analgesic effect in acetic acid-induced writhing in mice. Moreover, when given orally to rats at dose of 200 and 400 mg/kg, it showed a significant anti-inflammatory activity against carrageenin induced rat paw edema in rats.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
